[129.266514, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m5\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[129.26718, "o", "\r\u001b[2KNode.js is not installed in this environment, so I’ll avoid an unnecessary JavaScript build toolchain. A plain static site plus a small shell build step is more\r\nreliable, easier to audit, and works with GitHub Pages’ official deploy actions. Next I’ll create the site pages, shared styles/scripts, and the secure \r\nworkflow.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app/my_website && command -v nodejs || true; command -v rsync || true; command -v zip || true; printf '%s\\n' '--- disk ---'; df -h . | tail -1; printf \r\n'%s\\n' '--- initial tree ---'; find . -maxdepth 3 -type f -print | sort\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[129.267531, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[129.281096, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[129.281138, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n--- disk ---\r\noverlay         1.8T  1.5T  220G  88% /\r\n--- initial tree ---\r\n./.github/workflows/deploy.yml\r\n./info.md\r\n\r\n\u001b[92m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[?25l"]
