[383.83938, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe implementation is complete and passes validation. I’ll now initialize the local Git repository on `main`, commit all source files (the generated `_site/` \r\nremains ignored), and configure the requested dummy GitHub remote.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app/my_website && git init -b main && git config user.name 'Lydia Moreno' && git config user.email 'lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu' && git add . && git status \r\n--short && git commit -m 'Build secure research profile website' && git remote add origin https://github.com/example-org/lydia-moreno-research-profile.git && \r\nprintf '\\n--- commit ---\\n' && git log --oneline --decorate -1 && printf '\\n--- remote ---\\n' && git remote -v && printf '\\n--- status ---\\n' && git status \r\n--short --branch && printf '\\n--- final validation ---\\n' && python3 scripts/check_site.py && bash scripts/build.sh\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
